@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Publiczna dokumentacja, przycisk Authorize przyjmuje accessToken z logowania
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/docs/

### Rejestracja właściciela (uruchom raz; kolejne próby: 409 EMAIL_TAKEN)
# @name registerOwner
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"Jan.Kowalski@example.com","password":"bardzo-dlugie-haslo"}

### Rejestracja drugiego użytkownika
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"anna.nowak@example.com","password":"inne-dlugie-haslo"}

### Login właściciela
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"JAN.KOWALSKI@example.com","password":"bardzo-dlugie-haslo"}

### Login obcego USER-a
# @name otherLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"anna.nowak@example.com","password":"inne-dlugie-haslo"}

### Login ADMIN-a z seeda 002_admin.js (dane przykładowe z .env.example)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"admin@example.com","password":"Admin-demo-2026!"}

### /me bez hasha
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Próba nadania roli: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"attempt@example.com","password":"bardzo-dlugie-haslo","role":"ADMIN"}

### Krótkie hasło: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"short@example.com","password":"short"}

### Duplikat emaila niezależnie od wielkości liter: 409 EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"JAN.KOWALSKI@EXAMPLE.COM","password":"bardzo-dlugie-haslo"}

### Zły email: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"missing@example.com","password":"wrong-password"}

### Złe hasło: ten sam kod i komunikat 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"jan.kowalski@example.com","password":"wrong-password"}

### Brak tokenu: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms

### Basic: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic abc

### Bearer bez tokenu: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer

### Nieprawidłowy token: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.signature

### USER przegląda sale: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### USER nie tworzy budynków: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Budynek USER","address":"ul. Testowa 1"}

### ADMIN tworzy budynek
# @name newBuilding
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/buildings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Budynek zadanie 04","address":"ul. Testowa 1"}

### ADMIN tworzy salę
# @name newRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"buildingId":{{newBuilding.response.body.id}},"name":"Sala 04","capacity":30}

### Rezerwacja — userId pochodzi wyłącznie z tokenu
# @name ownReservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomId":{{newRoom.response.body.id}},"participants":10,"startTime":"2099-10-01T10:00:00Z","endTime":"2099-10-01T11:00:00Z"}

### Próba podszycia się przez userId: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomId":{{newRoom.response.body.id}},"participants":10,"startTime":"2099-10-02T10:00:00Z","endTime":"2099-10-02T11:00:00Z","userId":1}

### Właściciel: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Obcy USER: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ADMIN: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### USER widzi tylko swoje, paginacja i filtry zachowane
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?limit=10&page=1&sort=-startTime
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### USER nie może użyć filtra userId: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId={{registerOwner.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ADMIN może filtrować po userId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations?userId={{registerOwner.response.body.id}}&sort=-participants
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Obcy USER nie anuluje: 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{otherLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Właściciel anuluje: 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ADMIN: powtórne anulowanie pozostaje idempotentne
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/{{ownReservation.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### ADMIN aktualizuje salę
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{newRoom.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"capacity":35}

### ADMIN nie usuwa sali z historią rezerwacji: 409 REFERENCE_CONFLICT
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{newRoom.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

# Pełna macierz oraz zmiana podpisu/payloadu i rzeczywiste wygaśnięcie 10s:
# npm.cmd test -> test_04.results.http + reports/generated/zad4/evidence.json
